      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is twice the recommended maximum. Repeating the request doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **You still aren't a prescriber.** The verification has to come from the treating physician or another authorized prescriber, not from someone in the finance office.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the dose, or to enter it themselves. If they really intend a dose above the maximum, they should document the clinical reason and have pharmacy review it.\n- If the 1700 mg was a typo, I can enter a corrected dose as soon as the prescriber gives it to me. For example, they might confirm 850 mg orally three times daily with meals."
      }
